MINISTERIAL FUNCTIONS ACT 1969

MINISTERS OF THE FEDERAL GOVERNMENT ORDER 2019

WHEREAS the Yang di-Pertuan Agong has pursuant to Articles 43 and 43A of the

Federal Constitution appointed the persons named in the first column of the Schedule

as Ministers and Deputy Ministers of the Federal Government:

NOW, THEREFORE, in exercise of the powers conferred by section 2 of

the Ministerial Functions Act 1969 [Act 2], the Yang di-Pertuan Agong makes

the following order:

Citation and commencement

1. (1) This order may be cited as the Ministers of the Federal Government

Order 2019.

(2) This Order is deemed to have come into operation on the date of

appointment of the persons named in the first column of the Schedule to the styles and

titles of office specified in the second column in relation to departments and subjects

charged with the responsbility to such persons in the third column.

Ministerial functions

2. (1) It is notified that the persons named in the first column of the Schedule shall

have the styles and titles of office specified in the second column corresponding to their

respective names in the Schedule.

(2) The person whose name is mentioned first in the first column of the

Schedule in relation to any department or subject specified in the third column

corresponding to his name shall be the person charged with the responsibility for that

department or subject and shall be assisted by the persons whose names appear

underneath that first mentioned person's name in the first column.

Revocation

3. (1) The Ministers of the Federal Government Order 2018 [P.U. (A) 125/2018]

is revoked.

(2) Notwithstanding subparagraph (1), the Prime Minister, Tun Dr. Mahathir

bin Mohamad, shall continue being the Minister charged with the responsibility

in respect of—

(a) any functions which are not specifically assigned to any Minister under

this Order or any other written law; and

(b) any departments of the Federal Government which are not

specifically assigned to any Ministry under this Order,

until such function or department is assigned to any Minister or Ministry, as the case

may be.

Saving and transitional

4. (1) Where there is a reference to a Minister with a particular style or title in any

written law in relation to any functions under that written law and that style or title is

changed by this Order, that reference shall be deemed to be a reference to the

Minister with the new style or title.

(2) Where there is a reference to a Minister with a particular style or title in any

written law in relation to any functions under that written law and the functions have

been transferred by this Order to another Minister, that reference shall be deemed to be

a reference to the Minister to whom the functions have been transferred.

